-- title:
--   Elementary weight bound: $\log(|n|+3)/(1+n^2) \le 4\,|n|^{-3/2}$
-- statement:
--   **Statement.** For every nonzero integer $n$,
--   $$\frac{\log(|n| + 3)}{1 + n^2} \;\le\; 4\, |n|^{-3/2},$$
--   where $|n|^{-3/2}$ is the real power `|(n : ℝ)| ^ (-(3/2 : ℝ))`. An elementary calculus estimate: $\log(|n|+3) \le 4\sqrt{|n|}$ for $n \ne 0$, and $1 + n^2 \ge n^2$.
--
--   **Role.** In the module `Zeta23.WeilEF.ZeroSummability` this replaces the logarithmically-weighted unit-window counts by a summable power weight: it is the summand-level bound behind `zero_sum_inv_sq_gen`, the convergence of $\sum_\rho m_\rho / (1 + |\gamma_\rho|^2)$ over any zero configuration with a logarithmic local count.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/zeta-23-lean/blob/182afbf851aa42a8ae78507be83f2356d3a33260/Zeta23/WeilEF/ZeroSummability.lean#L39-L64

